 2. 🤖 AI gender gap 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Illustration: Aïda Amer/Axios. Stock: Getty Images Women are far more negative about AI than men are, Axios' Emily Peck writes from a new Morgan Stanley report. 

 By the numbers: Morgan Stanley polled 2,000 consumers in late September about their overall perception of AI, positive or negative. It then measured net sentiment (subtracting one from the other).

 Men were considerably more positive (+30%) than women (-1%) . 📊 44% of women said they don't want a data center built near their home, compared with 36% of men.

 👩‍💻 Slightly more women (57%) said they didn't like AI because "it is developing too quickly without enough safeguards." That's compared to 54% of men. Men were more likely to express concerns about data privacy (49% versus 39% of women). 

