 Residents board up an ice cream shop yesterday in Gulf Breeze, Fla. Photo: Joe Raedle/Getty Images 🌀 Hurricane Isaias strengthened into a major hurricane, with maximum sustained winds of 120 mph. Forecasters are warning of "life-threatening storm surge" from the mouth of the Mississippi River to Suwannee, Florida, plus damaging winds and power outages across the Gulf and inland. Latest forecast . 🏦 President Trump ordered a new investigation into allegations of mortgage fraud against Federal Reserve governor Lisa Cook, directing a committee to question the central bank official at a White House hearing next month. More from Courtenay Brown . 🎤 Vice President JD Vance said he won't be watching the execution of Fort Hood shooter Nidal Hasan if it is livestreamed. Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth said yesterday that the Dec. 3 execution by firing squad would be "public." More from Josephine Walker . 🕯️ Chicago sports icon Mike Ditka died today at 86 after years of health issues. The former Bears player and coach left a lasting impression on the city's sports and culture, presiding over one of the best teams in NFL history. More from Axios Chicago's Justin Kaufmann . 
 
